# Generated data and warehouses — rebuilt by `make data` / `make build`
data/*.csv
warehouse*.duckdb
# The sidecars DuckDB writes beside a database. `warehouse*.duckdb` does not
# match them, so a `git add -A` while a suite still held one open failed with
# "Permission denied" on the .wal — git was trying to index a file the engine
# had locked. They are as regenerable as the database itself.
*.duckdb.wal
*.duckdb.tmp/
*.duckdb.tmp

# Secrets and local configuration.
#
# .dockerignore has excluded these since the first image build; .gitignore did
# not, so a local .env full of real credentials was one `git add .` away from
# being published. tests/security_checks.py catches it, which is how this was
# found -- the gate is the reason the omission did not survive.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Terraform.
#
# State is the important one: it holds every generated password -- database
# roles, the Keycloak admin -- in PLAINTEXT. Anyone with the file has the
# warehouse. Local state is a deliberate student-tier choice (a remote backend
# needs a storage account that exists before Terraform runs), and gitignoring it
# is the other half of that decision. The enterprise path moves it into a
# storage account with restricted access; see azure/migration-to-enterprise.md.
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
# Real values, including subscription ids. The .example is the committed one.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# Environments
.venv*/
venv/
env/
# The interpreter directory a fresh checkout tends to create beside the code.
# `.venv*/` does not match a venv named after the project.
transfer-intelegence-platform/
transfer-intelligence-platform/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Console dependencies and build output — restored by `make web-install` from
# the committed package-lock.json, which is the pinned artefact, not the tree.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Local tooling state
.streamlit/
# Local AI-assistant configuration and generated metadata. These files are
# workstation-specific and must never be published with the application.
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.runtime/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: sql/, docs/, observability/grafana/, keycloak/.
# Dashboards, realms and metric definitions are provisioned from version control,
# never hand-edited in a running instance.

# Operator credential sheet, generated by scripts/credentials-sheet.ps1. Holds
# live secrets in plaintext for local convenience and must never be committed.
*.local.md
